Before it applies its sandbox, the AudioServer creates and discards an
AudioConverter, which gets AudioToolbox’s per-process code-signing check
done while F_GETPATH is still allowed. Run on macOS 27.3, a probe that
applies the AudioServer’s own generated profile and then initializes
CoreAudio’s default output unit crashed with SIGBUS in
AudioUnitInitialize(); with one AudioConverter created and discarded
before the profile went on, the unit initialized and started, under the
unchanged profile. The reporter’s macOS 14.8.7 log shows the same
denial, along with F_GETSIGSINFO and csrctl.

WebKit allows F_GETPATH (and F_GETSIGSINFO) in its GPU process, which
plays audio, in com.apple.WebKit.GPUProcess.sb. Chrome’s audio service
profile, audio.sb on top of common.sb, has no system-fcntl rules of its
own, and neither do Firefox’s macOS sandbox policies; this is from
reading their sources, not from running them.
